Design a test for the following execution path.

FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: insert
Signature: struct node* insert(struct node* node, int key)
Description: /**
 * @brief Insert a key into a binary search tree.
 *
 * Adds a new node with the specified key to the BST rooted at node,
 * preserving the binary search tree property. If the tree is empty
 * (node is NULL), creates and returns a new root node.
 *
 * @param node Root of the tree, or NULL for an empty tree. Not modified if key already exists.
 * @param key Key to insert into the tree.
 *
 * @return Root of the modified tree. Returns a newly allocated node if the tree was empty,
 *         or the existing root with the new node inserted.
 *
 * @note Caller is responsible for freeing the returned tree.
 * @see newNode
 */
Dependencies: insert, newNode

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
// C program for the function called insert
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

struct node {
	int key;
	struct node *left, *right;
};

// Forward declarations for dependency functions
struct node* newNode(int item);

// Target function implementation
struct node* insert(struct node* node, int key)
{

	if (node == NULL)
		return newNode(key);


	if (key < node->key)
		node->left = insert(node->left, key);
	else
		node->right = insert(node->right, key);

	return node;
}

```

TARGET EXECUTION PATH:
Path 3: START | START --> CONDITION | if-else head --> STATEMENT | (node == NULL) --> RETURN | return newNode(key);

IMPORTANT: Choose inputs that satisfy this path's conditions.

